abstract: 'We construct natural-number arithmetic on an ordered family of correlation modes
  and retain the expressions by which its elements are generated. Minimal unbiased compositional
  change determines a rotation plane and a Gaussian law. Local information and total normalized
  correlation determine a finite window; preservation of constants selects its Neumann closure
  within the separated homogeneous local boundary class. Modulation and composition of the oriented
  modes define an ordered Peano semiring with unique factorization. The modes retain quadratic
  energy and canonical scale transport, while winding degree certifies the arithmetic. Ordered
  expressions have finite evaluation fibres. Equal root-channel weights and independent subhistory
  assembly determine a positive history law whose Gaussian marginal is the original mode mass.
  Conditional readout separates value information from internal history variation by exact variance
  and entropy identities. Using the same weights, parent–child assembly defines a nonnegative
  self-adjoint trace-class operator with explicit Gaussian cutoff bounds. Its contraction evolution
  couples value coefficients to history differences with zero initial readout: an exact matrix
  element at value four proves this coupling on the complete history space. The coupling persists
  under small changes of the relevant conditional weights. Eliminating the history differences
  gives an exact integral equation for the value response. Lean formalizations accompany the
  arithmetic construction, history-source recursion and assembly results.'
